# The changelog is append-only replication (D-15): one INSERT per line, each
# guarded by ON CONFLICT, so the union of two branches is the correct merge and
# a conflict here is noise. Two clones filing tickets in parallel is the normal
# case, not an edge one.
#
# The pattern needs `**` because the changelog is per-table subdirectories —
# `.pql/changelog/tickets/2026-09.sql`, not `.pql/changelog/2026-09.sql`. The
# original rule was written against the flat layout and kept matching nothing
# after the split, so every parallel filing conflicted by hand instead.
.pql/changelog/**/*.sql merge=union
